      <Comment source="chawkins, SRI, caspi">|FRAME: CPD-12380 Pheomelanin| is a common type of melanin pigment, which is found in hair and skin. Pheomelanin imparts a pink to red hue and is accordingly found in large quantities in red hair. In skin pheomelanin is particularly concentrated in the lips, nipples, glans of the penis, and vagina.</Comment>
